From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:04:59 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 52/79] flashnext_mia: host tests for the lane under
 TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia, her lanes holding

test-flashnext-mia-host now runs three more native tests:

- her family declares upstream flashnext's compute and runner bindings,
  the declarations openWith boots the lane and opens the runner from;
- the ML arm (TF_COMPUTE_LANE=1, _DEFAULT=1, TF_RUNNER=0) and the MR arm
  (the graph-bank runner, S3 on TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER*) parse through
  them: the lane's default, the runner's forms and knobs, Qwen's quiet
  spans and never-owned markup, S3's circuit, bank and settle time;
- her lane backend (Lanes over her Toy engine) under the real LaneHost:
  two replies held at their EOS, resumed with results that hold the EOS
  (ChatML's <|im_end|>), land every result row and draw on, each drawn
  token her target's greedy one over the whole history. Drafted, drafts
  off, and a backend without a head; two streams a forward.

Her module root exports cuda_lanes.zig as lane_backend for that test.
